---
import Layout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentGuide from "@/components/Item/ContentGuide.astro";
const content = {
  eyebrow: "Privacy & trust",
  title: "A boundary you can understand.",
  intro:
    "Your files and index stay on your computer. AI and web search have explicit destinations. Understand what each choice sends outside the installation.",
  sections: [
    {
      id: "local",
      title: "Your index stays with your installation",
      paragraphs: [
        "KeepIndex stores extracted file text, imported browser metadata, settings, search history, and evidence records in local SQLite and browser storage. Original files remain in the selected folders.",
        "The public product website has no connection to these stores. There is no hosted indexing service or KeepIndex account. Remote AI is an explicit endpoint choice, separate from where your index lives.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "ai",
      title: "Local AI by default. Remote AI by choice.",
      paragraphs: [
        "With a local runtime, prompts and evidence go to that runtime on this computer. If you select Blade or another remote endpoint, prompts, conversation context, and retrieved excerpts go there for AI processing. Source folders and the database remain here.",
        "The app labels each connection as local or remote and shows the active connection beside the query box. No automatic fallback switches between connections. API keys stay in an owner-readable file on your installation, not in browser storage or the website. Endpoint redirects and credentials embedded in URLs are rejected.",
        "You control the chosen runtime or gateway. Its own logging, retention, forwarding, and model-provider settings apply to the content you send it. Use a locally executing runtime when that content must remain on the computer.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "web",
      title: "Web searches leave the computer",
      paragraphs: [
        "All and Web queries send search terms through your local SearXNG instance to public engines. Source hydration can fetch webpages. Engines and websites can see the requests they receive.",
        "Files, Vaults, Docs, and History retrieve their local source category without web discovery. Do not include secrets in web-enabled queries. Opening an external result or following a cited website also makes a normal internet request.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "storage",
      title: "Local does not mean encrypted",
      paragraphs: [
        "KeepIndex does not encrypt its SQLite index, browser storage, or exported backups. Use a protected OS account, disk encryption, and appropriate backup storage. Exports can contain private text.",
        "The personal API has no user authentication. Loopback publication and origin checks protect the local application boundary; they do not isolate you from another OS user or malicious software already running on the computer.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "control",
      title: "Grant, inspect, remove",
      paragraphs: [
        "Containers read only the folders you mount. Browser-history imports require selected profiles. Secret-like files and hidden folders are excluded by default, but these filters cannot identify every sensitive passage inside an ordinary document.",
        "Remove resources to delete their index entries, clear imported history, or reset KeepIndex state in Settings. Original files and original browser databases are not deleted.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "answers",
      title: "Citations are for inspection",
      paragraphs: [
        "KeepIndex checks citation identifiers and coverage and applies lexical checks during repair. Insufficient grounding can prevent an answer from being recorded as a grounded success.",
        "These are engineering checks, not factual verification. An answer can be mistaken even when its citation resolves. Inspect the underlying source when the decision matters.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "website",
      title: "This public website",
      paragraphs: [
        "keepindex.ing is a static product website hosted on Blade through Cloudflare. Cloudflare and the web host process normal visitor request metadata to deliver it. The site has no added analytics scripts or private-device connection.",
        "The interactive example contains sample data and makes no search or inference requests. External links, including GitHub, have their own privacy practices. Phone access displays this website, not a private KeepIndex instance.",
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={content.title} description={content.intro}
  ><ContentGuide {...content} /></Layout
>
